  "question": {
    "text": "A printed page is pressed by a glass of water. The refractive index of the glass and water is $1.5$ and $1.33$, respectively. If the thickness of the bottom of glass is $1 \\mathrm{~cm}$ and depth of water is $5 \\mathrm{~cm}$, how much the page will appear to be shifted if viewed from the top ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CCDVl",
      "text": "\n$1.033 \\mathrm{~cm}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4peKW",
      "text": "\n$3.581 \\mathrm{~cm}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KrOpg",
      "text": "\n$1.3533 \\mathrm{~cm}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "xHkiz",
      "text": "\n$1.90 \\mathrm{~cm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Real depth $=5 \\mathrm{~cm}+1 \\mathrm{~cm}=6 \\mathrm{~cm}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/vi1LONKyrZMhZRLmiPx905jEDfZ1NxZfkPxrIUZRDL8.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nApparent depth $=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}_1}{\\mu_1}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}_2}{\\mu_2}+\\ldots$\n$=\\frac{5}{1.33}+\\frac{1}{1.5}$\n$\\simeq 3.8+0.7 \\simeq 4.5 \\mathrm{~cm}$\n$\\therefore$ Shift $=6 \\mathrm{~cm}-4.5 \\mathrm{~cm} \\cong 1.5 \\mathrm{~cm}$",
    "image": null
  },
